OpenSSH server and service

Install:
  Install OpenSSH server; enable and start the service on a new installation.

Upgrade:
  Update the installed OpenSSH server, preserving its startup settings.

Status:
  Report the installed package version, service activity, and startup state.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a running systemd instance; root or sudo.

Configuration:
  Server configuration: /etc/ssh/sshd_config and its included files; authentication and server settings remain administrator-managed.
